    },
    {
      "id": "comorbidity_safety_filter",
      "text": "Before choosing, filter options through stated comorbidities. If a condition such as hypertension, arrhythmia, or hypotension is present, prefer agents with a favorable profile for that condition and avoid drugs that could worsen it."
    },
    {
      "id": "indication_over_familiarity",
      "text": "Match the option to the specific diagnosis implied by the full symptom cluster, not to the most familiar drug in the class. A drug that is generally used for a related condition may be wrong if the patient's presentation points to a narrower indication."
    },
    {
      "id": "same_class_safer_alternative",
      "text": "When two options are in the same therapeutic class, choose the one with the better safety profile for this patient's comorbidity or current medication, rather than the more commonly used or more potent member of the class."
    },
    {
      "id": "absent_fact_not_permission",
      "text": "Do not treat a missing contraindication, interaction, or allergy as if it were absent. If the patient has not been asked about a relevant safety fact, do not assume it is safe; prefer the option that is least likely to cause harm given what is known."
    },
    {
      "id": "adjunct_vs_first_line",
      "text": "Distinguish first-line treatment from adjunct or rescue therapy. If the diagnosis calls for initial immunosuppression or replacement therapy, do not choose a drug that is typically added later or used only in non-responders."
